meta {
  name: Generate Query
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/azure-ai/generate-query
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "connectionId": "{{connectionId}}",
    "prompt": "Show the 10 most recent orders",
    "currentQuery": "",
    "refreshSchema": false,
    "mode": "read",
    "schema": "public"
  }
}

docs {
  Generate a query from natural language. `mode`: read | write. The model receives schema metadata plus, while the AI setting `columnValues` is on (default; see Get AI Settings), the distinct values of short text columns with at most 20 values that no PHI rule matches. Never PHI, never query results or other row data. A request Azure's content filter blocks returns 422 with a "try rephrasing" message.

  Requires a valid Bearer JWT ({{token}}) plus **read** capability for the connection's environment — 403 otherwise (admins hold every environment).
}
